\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every prime $p$, positive chromatic height $n\ge1$, and integer degree $k$, must $\pi_kL_{K(n)}S^0$ be a finitely generated module over the $p$-adic integers? Here $L_{K(n)}$ is localization of the sphere spectrum at the height-$n$ Morava $K$-theory.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~tlawson/hovey/}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
